\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) $C_{11}$ of \textit  {bcc} Fe$_{1-x}$Cr$_x$: literature calculations of Razumovskiy \textit  {et al.} \cite  {razumovskiy2011first} (black circles; reconstructed from digitized $C'$, $C_{44}$, and $B$), present DFT calculations on 40-atom SQS with VASP (filled red diamonds) and Quantum ESPRESSO at the PBE-relaxed lattice parameter (open diamonds) and at the experimental lattice parameter (filled blue diamonds; 5--50 and 95\% Cr) (SM S3), MD (EAM) random alloys (green squares; mean $\pm $ standard deviation of ten alloys at the DFT compositions and three elsewhere; Sec.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:md}), and fully decomposed MD structures ($\phi =1$, open squares; $25^3$ cells). (b) Orientation-resolved acoustic frequencies at $\lambda =6.4\,\mu $m, plotted at the $C_{11}$ of each tensor in (a). For each tensor, 10{,}000 random grain orientations were computed with the surface Green's-function method of Du and Zhao \cite  {du2017facile}, as in Ref.\nobreakspace  {}\cite  {al2023detecting}. Lower violins: (pseudo-)SAW frequencies (pseudo-SAW retained when its intensity is at least $2\times 10^{-3}$ of the SAW). Upper violins: quasi-longitudinal bulk waves along the same propagation directions. Boxes mark the interquartile range and median. The shaded band is the elastodynamically unallowed range of pristine 304-type CASS \cite  {al2023detecting}, from its maximum (pseudo-)SAW frequency (0.609 GHz, dashed) to its bulk-wave frequency (0.833 GHz, dotted). (c) The MD cells behind the green tensors, viewed as whole $25^3$ cells (three outer faces): random alloy and fully decomposed structure at $x_{\mathrm  {Cr}}=0.20$, 0.36, and 0.50 (red, Fe; blue, Cr). Panel (b) shows both QE sets, in the colours of (a).\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:elastic_elastodynamics}{{2}{5}{(a) $C_{11}$ of \textit {bcc} Fe$_{1-x}$Cr$_x$: literature calculations of Razumovskiy \textit {et al.} \cite {razumovskiy2011first} (black circles; reconstructed from digitized $C'$, $C_{44}$, and $B$), present DFT calculations on 40-atom SQS with VASP (filled red diamonds) and Quantum ESPRESSO at the PBE-relaxed lattice parameter (open diamonds) and at the experimental lattice parameter (filled blue diamonds; 5--50 and 95\% Cr) (SM S3), MD (EAM) random alloys (green squares; mean $\pm $ standard deviation of ten alloys at the DFT compositions and three elsewhere; Sec.~\ref {sec:md}), and fully decomposed MD structures ($\phi =1$, open squares; $25^3$ cells). (b) Orientation-resolved acoustic frequencies at $\lambda =6.4\,\mu $m, plotted at the $C_{11}$ of each tensor in (a). For each tensor, 10{,}000 random grain orientations were computed with the surface Green's-function method of Du and Zhao \cite {du2017facile}, as in Ref.~\cite {al2023detecting}. Lower violins: (pseudo-)SAW frequencies (pseudo-SAW retained when its intensity is at least $2\times 10^{-3}$ of the SAW). Upper violins: quasi-longitudinal bulk waves along the same propagation directions. Boxes mark the interquartile range and median. The shaded band is the elastodynamically unallowed range of pristine 304-type CASS \cite {al2023detecting}, from its maximum (pseudo-)SAW frequency (0.609 GHz, dashed) to its bulk-wave frequency (0.833 GHz, dotted). (c) The MD cells behind the green tensors, viewed as whole $25^3$ cells (three outer faces): random alloy and fully decomposed structure at $x_{\mathrm {Cr}}=0.20$, 0.36, and 0.50 (red, Fe; blue, Cr). Panel (b) shows both QE sets, in the colours of (a).\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
