\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces (a) The enthalpy of mixing demonstrates the thermodynamic drive towards phase separation indicative of spinodal decomposition, affecting the material's mechanical integrity. (b) Variations in the melting temperature as a function of Cr composition offer insights into the thermal stability and potential phase transformations within the alloy. The melting temperature is the Lindemann estimate $T_m=0.00321\,f^2 M V^{2/3}\Theta _D^2$ ($M$ in g/mol, $V$ in cm$^3$/mol) from the present VASP tensors, with $\Theta _D$ from the Debye average of the VRH sound speeds and the Lindemann constant $f$ calibrated on the measured melting points of Fe (1811\nobreakspace  {}K) and Cr (2180\nobreakspace  {}K); this corrects the original panel, which used Planck's constant in place of $k_B$ and the arithmetic mean of the sound speeds. (c) Changes in Rayleigh wave frequencies across compositions highlight alterations in surface acoustic properties, correlating with mechanical behavior. (d) The Embrittlement (Pugh) Criterion allows for assessing the risk of material embrittlement due to changes in composition, crucial for ensuring material reliability in critical applications.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig3}{{S5}{15}{(a) The enthalpy of mixing demonstrates the thermodynamic drive towards phase separation indicative of spinodal decomposition, affecting the material's mechanical integrity. (b) Variations in the melting temperature as a function of Cr composition offer insights into the thermal stability and potential phase transformations within the alloy. The melting temperature is the Lindemann estimate $T_m=0.00321\,f^2 M V^{2/3}\Theta _D^2$ ($M$ in g/mol, $V$ in cm$^3$/mol) from the present VASP tensors, with $\Theta _D$ from the Debye average of the VRH sound speeds and the Lindemann constant $f$ calibrated on the measured melting points of Fe (1811~K) and Cr (2180~K); this corrects the original panel, which used Planck's constant in place of $k_B$ and the arithmetic mean of the sound speeds. (c) Changes in Rayleigh wave frequencies across compositions highlight alterations in surface acoustic properties, correlating with mechanical behavior. (d) The Embrittlement (Pugh) Criterion allows for assessing the risk of material embrittlement due to changes in composition, crucial for ensuring material reliability in critical applications.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{RF2}{16}
\newlabel{fig4a}{{S6a}{16}{Predicted elastic frequencies showcasing the emergence of new modes within the elastodynamically-unallowed regions, signifying alterations in the material's mechanical properties due to spinodal decomposition.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig4a}{{a}{16}{Predicted elastic frequencies showcasing the emergence of new modes within the elastodynamically-unallowed regions, signifying alterations in the material's mechanical properties due to spinodal decomposition.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig4b}{{S6b}{16}{Calculated acoustic frequencies across different Cr compositions, illustrating the material's acoustic response variability with composition. This graph provides a quantitative measure of the material's mechanical behavior and its dependence on the microstructural characteristics induced by varying chromium content.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig4b}{{b}{16}{Calculated acoustic frequencies across different Cr compositions, illustrating the material's acoustic response variability with composition. This graph provides a quantitative measure of the material's mechanical behavior and its dependence on the microstructural characteristics induced by varying chromium content.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig4c}{{S6c}{16}{Measured elastic moduli distribution from experimental data, highlighting the range and variability of material properties within stainless steel samples subjected to different thermal aging processes. The distribution underscores the significant impact of microstructural changes, such as spinodal decomposition, on the material's overall stiffness and mechanical integrity.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig4c}{{c}{16}{Measured elastic moduli distribution from experimental data, highlighting the range and variability of material properties within stainless steel samples subjected to different thermal aging processes. The distribution underscores the significant impact of microstructural changes, such as spinodal decomposition, on the material's overall stiffness and mechanical integrity.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S6}{\ignorespaces (a) Quantum elastodynamic frequencies obtained from density functional theory calculations reveal the complex interplay between microstructural evolution and mechanical properties in stainless steels undergoing spinodal decomposition. These findings are corroborated by (b) calculated acoustic frequencies that vary with Cr composition, providing a link between composition, microstructure, and acoustic properties. (c) The distribution of measured elastic moduli further validates the theoretical predictions, illustrating the broad impact of aging and compositional changes on the material's mechanical performance.\relax }}{16}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig4}{{S6}{16}{(a) Quantum elastodynamic frequencies obtained from density functional theory calculations reveal the complex interplay between microstructural evolution and mechanical properties in stainless steels undergoing spinodal decomposition. These findings are corroborated by (b) calculated acoustic frequencies that vary with Cr composition, providing a link between composition, microstructure, and acoustic properties. (c) The distribution of measured elastic moduli further validates the theoretical predictions, illustrating the broad impact of aging and compositional changes on the material's mechanical performance.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{RF3}{17}
\newlabel{fig5a}{{S7a}{17}{Experimental elastic moduli of aged steels, displaying how aging temperature influences the material's stiffness. This graph illustrates the correlation between thermal treatment and the increase in elastic moduli, indicative of the material's response to microstructural changes over time.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5a}{{a}{17}{Experimental elastic moduli of aged steels, displaying how aging temperature influences the material's stiffness. This graph illustrates the correlation between thermal treatment and the increase in elastic moduli, indicative of the material's response to microstructural changes over time.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig5b}{{S7b}{17}{Theoretical elastic moduli of pristine steels, offering a baseline comparison for understanding how spinodal decomposition affects material properties before and after aging. This comparison elucidates the stiffening effect of microstructural evolution on the alloy's mechanical behavior.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5b}{{b}{17}{Theoretical elastic moduli of pristine steels, offering a baseline comparison for understanding how spinodal decomposition affects material properties before and after aging. This comparison elucidates the stiffening effect of microstructural evolution on the alloy's mechanical behavior.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig5c}{{S7c}{17}{Theoretical elastic moduli of spinodally decomposed steels, demonstrating the pronounced impact of microstructural evolution on the alloy's stiffness. This direct comparison to pristine conditions highlights the significant role of chromium composition and thermal aging in material performance.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5c}{{c}{17}{Theoretical elastic moduli of spinodally decomposed steels, demonstrating the pronounced impact of microstructural evolution on the alloy's stiffness. This direct comparison to pristine conditions highlights the significant role of chromium composition and thermal aging in material performance.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig5d}{{S7d}{17}{\(D^{exp}_{thermal}\), experimental thermal diffusivity as measured in aged stainless steel, illustrating the thermal transport characteristics and their variation with temperature. This metric provides insights into the thermal stability and heat dissipation capabilities of the material post-aging.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5d}{{d}{17}{\(D^{exp}_{thermal}\), experimental thermal diffusivity as measured in aged stainless steel, illustrating the thermal transport characteristics and their variation with temperature. This metric provides insights into the thermal stability and heat dissipation capabilities of the material post-aging.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig5e}{{S7e}{17}{\(D^{theoretical}_{thermal}\), theoretical thermal diffusivity indicating the expected thermal behavior based on composition and microstructural considerations. This predictive analysis aids in understanding the thermal management potential of the alloy across a range of compositions.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5e}{{e}{17}{\(D^{theoretical}_{thermal}\), theoretical thermal diffusivity indicating the expected thermal behavior based on composition and microstructural considerations. This predictive analysis aids in understanding the thermal management potential of the alloy across a range of compositions.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig5f}{{S7f}{17}{\(\kappa ^{theoretical}_{thermal}\), thermal conductivity, showcasing the theoretical prediction of how efficiently the material conducts heat. This property is crucial for applications where thermal management is key, and it is influenced by the alloy's microstructure and composition.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig5f}{{f}{17}{\(\kappa ^{theoretical}_{thermal}\), thermal conductivity, showcasing the theoretical prediction of how efficiently the material conducts heat. This property is crucial for applications where thermal management is key, and it is influenced by the alloy's microstructure and composition.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces Comprehensive analysis combining experimental and theoretical insights into the thermal and mechanical properties of stainless steels subjected to thermal aging. (a) Experimental elastic moduli trends with aging temperature highlight the stiffening effect of microstructural evolution. (b) and (c) Theoretical predictions for pristine and spinodally decomposed steels provide a comparative framework for assessing the impact of spinodal decomposition on material properties. (d) Experimental thermal diffusivity measurements, alongside (e) theoretical predictions for thermal diffusivity and (f) thermal conductivity, offer a holistic view of the material's thermal and mechanical behavior post-aging, emphasizing the interconnectedness of thermal properties, mechanical performance, and microstructural characteristics.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig5}{{S7}{17}{Comprehensive analysis combining experimental and theoretical insights into the thermal and mechanical properties of stainless steels subjected to thermal aging. (a) Experimental elastic moduli trends with aging temperature highlight the stiffening effect of microstructural evolution. (b) and (c) Theoretical predictions for pristine and spinodally decomposed steels provide a comparative framework for assessing the impact of spinodal decomposition on material properties. (d) Experimental thermal diffusivity measurements, alongside (e) theoretical predictions for thermal diffusivity and (f) thermal conductivity, offer a holistic view of the material's thermal and mechanical behavior post-aging, emphasizing the interconnectedness of thermal properties, mechanical performance, and microstructural characteristics.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
