\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S24}{\ignorespaces Electronic topological transition on the Fe-rich side. (a) Critical level $z=E_{\mathrm  F}-E_c$ (majority level at H) from our band structures: pure Fe at both lattice parameters and the unfolded 5 and 10\%\nobreakspace  {}Cr SQS at the experimental lattice parameter (error bars: disorder spread of the spectral weight). The line through the experimental-lattice points gives $x_c=0.079$ (dashed; light band: $\pm $ spread). (b--d) $C_{44}$, $B$ and $f_{\mathrm  {SAW}}$: EMTO-CPA \cite  {razumovskiy2011first} (black) with the joint fit of Eq.\nobreakspace  {}(\ref  {eq:ett_fit}), measured bulk moduli (red triangles, \cite  {korzhavyi2009electronic}) and our QE SQS (open symbols). The grey band is the joint-fit range of $x_c$. (e) $\Delta \chi ^2$ of the joint fit against the onset $x_c$; triangles mark the model-independent anomaly positions (red: measured). (f) Lever-rule stiffening of Fe--36Cr (CALPHAD phase compositions at 748\nobreakspace  {}K), split into the Fe-rich $\alpha $ and Cr-rich $\alpha '$ terms, for the electronic and classical $f_{\mathrm  {SAW}}(x)$. Script: \texttt  {dft\_qe/ett\_analysis.py}.\relax }}{31}{figure.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:S_ett}{{S24}{31}{Electronic topological transition on the Fe-rich side. (a) Critical level $z=E_{\mathrm F}-E_c$ (majority level at H) from our band structures: pure Fe at both lattice parameters and the unfolded 5 and 10\%~Cr SQS at the experimental lattice parameter (error bars: disorder spread of the spectral weight). The line through the experimental-lattice points gives $x_c=0.079$ (dashed; light band: $\pm $ spread). (b--d) $C_{44}$, $B$ and $f_{\mathrm {SAW}}$: EMTO-CPA \cite {razumovskiy2011first} (black) with the joint fit of Eq.~(\ref {eq:ett_fit}), measured bulk moduli (red triangles, \cite {korzhavyi2009electronic}) and our QE SQS (open symbols). The grey band is the joint-fit range of $x_c$. (e) $\Delta \chi ^2$ of the joint fit against the onset $x_c$; triangles mark the model-independent anomaly positions (red: measured). (f) Lever-rule stiffening of Fe--36Cr (CALPHAD phase compositions at 748~K), split into the Fe-rich $\alpha $ and Cr-rich $\alpha '$ terms, for the electronic and classical $f_{\mathrm {SAW}}(x)$. Script: \texttt {dft\_qe/ett\_analysis.py}.\relax }{figure.caption.41}{}}
